Redistribution
--------------

A compiled build of this project contains the game's own code, translated.
That is why the framework's documentation says generated sources are derived
from your disc and must not be redistributed — and a binary built from them is
that same material in compiled form.

Sharing the *project* (this repository) is a different thing from sharing a
*build*, and it is the safer one: a recipient supplies their own disc, runs the
recompiler against it, and builds locally. That flow is what the packaging in
`scripts/package_setup_release.sh` is designed around.

Use only a disc image and BIOS you obtained legally.
